  `n = Ke, m = Kd`, `[h,g] = e f^{e−1}[f,g]` gives `deg h ≥ K(de−d−e)+2` (the bound in
  the charge). In the `η`-gauge, `deg_y h = (e−1)m − j_0` where
  `j_0 = min{ j > −m : f_j ≠ 0 }`, so the Jacobian bound reads `j_0 ≤ n−2` — a
