+# Blind ideation submission - round 20260903T1200Z - GPT-5.5
+
+## 0. Custody, blindness, and thesis
+
+The charged packet hash was verified before reading campaign material:
+
+`c90fa6876b069478f658845be6efa2bd056b2e340af7284104af4d042e6c4f95  /tmp/jc2-lane.3XG5jb/inputs/ideation-20260903T1200Z-packet.md`
+
+I read the sealed packet first. I then read only banked or final reports as needed:
+`AUDIT.md` deltas 17(p)-17(t), `APPROACHES.md`, the latest LIVE STATE / EVENT
+blocks in `notes.md`, `xmodel/ideation-20260903T1015Z-synthesis.md`,
+`xmodel/moh-program-review-sol56-20260903.md`,
+`xmodel/whole-tree-review-grok46-20260903.md`,
+`xmodel/m2-descent-opus5-20260903.md`,
+`xmodel/descent-radii-grok46-20260903.md`,
+`xmodel/ps-growth-opus5-20260903.md`, and the final/sealed
+`xmodel/a2six-ray-moment-sol56-20260903.md`. I checked `.run.v2` before
+opening current-lane reports. I did not read any same-round
+`ideation-20260903T1200Z-*` submission other than the packet. I did not read
+the `.md` reports for running lanes without `final_status=DONE`; in particular,
+I did not open the in-progress `whole-tree-review-opus5`,
+`screened-census-grok46`, or `sibling-coefficients-sol56` reports. I did not
+edit canonical ledgers. I did not inspect `jc2-lean`.
+
+No new exit-price assertion is made in this report, so no `charge_basis` line
+is declared.
+
+My direct answer: the coordinator's framing is essentially right after AUDIT
+17(r), but it is underspecified in one important way. The boundary computes
+candidate `N`; the full major tree computes the admissible multiplicity
+structure; the remaining freedom is coefficient realisability. The mistake
+would be to treat the new all-degree program as "prove the screened census is
+eventually empty" or as "push the moment engine on bare skeletons." The all-degree
+program should now be:
+
+1. Use `C_FULL_TREE` / `C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` as the non-negotiable front-end.
+2. Build the sibling coefficient compiler for the first live `D=108` group.
+3. Feed any surviving decorated local data into the theorem-(T) / Appendix-II
+   monomial-Jacobian compiler.
+4. Run the tree-decorated moment engine only after the route-to-tree coefficient
+   dictionary exists.
+
+If the coefficient compiler empties the first `D=108` group for a structural
+reason, that reason is the first plausible route to an all-degree theorem. If it
+does not, it gives the strongest counterexample attack the campaign has had
+since the D=105/D=117 front collapsed.
+
+## 1. Binding state and a desk-scale census check
+
+The promoted state I am using is:
+
+- Moh arithmetic conditions (1)-(13) are necessary screens, not existence.
+- The whole-major-tree obligation is promoted: every above-threshold sibling
+  factor must be accounted for, not only the selected path.
+- `C_FULL_TREE` is necessary. `C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` is a stronger screened
+  necessary filter with current empirical force, not a proof of sharpness.
+- D=105 and D=117 are empty on the promoted screened census. Both fixed-N rays
+  from the morning are dead.
+- D=108 is the first live degree after the rebasing: 18 rows, 11 groups, 8
+  pinned-N alive groups under the full-tree/passport screen.
+- The descent-radii formula is now closed and matches Moh p.207 examples.
+- `M2 > m` is not a theorem for Keller pairs in Moh gauge; use it only as a
+  conditional/programmatic fork if the source hypotheses actually imply it.
+- PS-growth gives useful exact trace/remainder arithmetic and branch-growth
+  shapes, but it does not give a degree ceiling.
+- Bare moment matrices on the A2=6 ray were the wrong target after the tree
+  rebasing; they become controls for a tree-decorated moment engine.
+
+I ran only small desk-scale census queries against the local drivers/results.
+They confirm the promoted counts:
+
+- D=105: no `C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` survivors.
+- D=117: no `C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` survivors.
+- D=108: 18 survivor rows, 11 survivor groups, 8 groups with a pinned `N >= 6`.
+
+The concrete first coefficient target should be the D=108 group
+
+`(n,m,D)=(108,72,36), M=(24,78,106), V4=5`.
+
+It has two survivor rows sharing the same top node but using opposite
+zero/nonzero decisions below:
+
+- Row A: `V={2:1,3:1,4:5}`, `q=1/2`, `u=30`,
+  `delta=(7/12,5/12,1/6,-1)`, `A=(1,2,6)`. At `j=3`,
+  `(P,Q,A,b)=(10,25,6,4)` with a zero sibling of multiplicity 4 and one
+  nonzero orbit of multiplicity 1. The selected child then has
+  `(P,Q,A,b)=(3,7,2,1)` and selects the zero child after danger has been
+  cleared by the nonzero step.
+- Row B: `V={2:1,3:4,4:5}`, `q=2/3`, `u=30`,
+  `delta=(4/9,2/9,1/6,-1)`, `A=(1,3,6)`. At `j=3` the same
+  `(P,Q,A,b)=(10,25,6,4)` appears, but the selected child is zero and danger
+  remains. At `j=2`, `(P,Q,A,b)=(12,28,3,0)` uses four nonzero orbits of
+  multiplicity 1.
+
+This is the new cross-connection I would force into the next lane: the first
+post-rebase survivor lives by alternating zero and nonzero major-tree choices.
+The coefficient system must decide whether "danger clearing by a nonzero orbit,
+then selected zero" is real or only a tree-level artifact.
+
+## 2. Disposition over Q1-Q4
+
+### Q1 - screened census cofinality
+
+Disposition: `REDESIGN / CONTINUE AS SECONDARY`.
+
+Do not make the all-degree program wait on a pure census theorem. The D=105 and
+D=117 empty results are strong evidence that full-tree bookkeeping was the
+missing boundary-level constraint, but D=108 being live says the pure tree is
+not currently a proof. The best Q1 task is to find the first symbolic
+explanation of empty blocks: the forced `b_min = P mod A2 > h` mechanism. If
+that mechanism can be lifted from the killed fixed-N rays to every large
+screened row, excellent. If it cannot, the census still supplies coefficient
+targets.
+
+OPEN raised: `OPEN[SCREENED-COFINALITY]`.
+
+Bounded quantity: exact survivor counts for `C_FULL_TREE` and
+`C_FULL_TREE_PASSPORT` through `D <= 400`, grouped by `(n,m,M,V)` and by
+minimal pinned `N`, plus any affine-linear family of survivor groups.
+
+Cheapest test: finish the running screened census with the promoted
+full-tree/passport driver; if it finds a family, verify the symbolic
+`P,A,b,h` recurrences on the family. If it finds long empty bands, extract the
+common inequality template before expanding degree range.
+
+### Q2 - coefficient level, theorem (T), and tree-decorated moments
+
+Disposition: `RAISE TO PRIMARY`.
+
+Q2 is now the frontier. The right coefficient problem is not "fit one selected
+path." It is simultaneous sibling realisability over one coefficient field,
+with node-local `p_j,q_j` satisfying Moh A.3 and the full major tree's
+multiplicity choices. The theorem-(T) monomial-Jacobian statement is the
+terminal local form of the same obstruction, while tree-decorated moments are
+the global interpolation form after the local dictionary is known.
+
+Candidate disposition:
+
+- `sibling coefficient compiler`: `CONTINUE / FIRST HARVEST`. Its first target
+  must be the D=108 group above, not a dead D=105 or ray instance.
+- `theorem (T) compiler`: `RAISE`. Use descent-radii closure and Appendix-II
+  controls to compile exact monomial-Jacobian systems.
+- `tree-decorated moment engine`: `REDESIGN THEN CONTINUE`. It needs route
+  decoration and legal nonproper value columns; bare consecutive moment
+  matrices are not intrinsic.
+- `P202 residue front`: `REDESIGN`. Run it only after the sibling compiler has
+  emitted a coefficient dictionary or a canonical unsat certificate.
+
+OPEN raised: `OPEN[SIBLING-COEFFICIENTS]`.
+
+Bounded quantity: for the D=108 group above, solve the two adjacent node systems
+in cyclic quotient variables: top `(P,Q,A,b)=(10,25,6,4)`, then row-A child
+`(3,7,2,1)` and row-B child `(12,28,3,0)`, with common leading-term and
+coefficient-field gluing.
+
+Cheapest test: implement the A.3 cyclic-quotient normal form in `z=pi^A`,
+solve top and child systems separately over a small rational/modular ladder,
+then glue constants. A unit ideal kills the first live group; an exact witness
+feeds the tree-decorated moment engine. This is comfortably desk-scale if the
+quotient is used before Groebner.
+
+### Q3 - descent and theorem (T)
+
+Disposition: `RAISE, BUT DO NOT CONFUSE WITH M2>m`.
+
+The descent reports changed the role of Q3. The false lead is "prove `M2 > m`."
+That is refuted as a theorem in Moh gauge by explicit automorphism witnesses.
+The productive statement is theorem (T): no monomial-Jacobian pair, monic in
+`pi`, of the descended data and `J=c gamma^k`, exists for any screened skeleton.
+The descent-radii formula now removes a major ambiguity; G2/G3 at D=105 are
+calibration cases, not live frontier rows.
+
+Candidate disposition:
+
+- `M2 > m`: `STOP AS THEOREM`, keep only as source-hypothesis conditional.
+- `G2/G3 D=105 descended systems`: `CONTINUE AS CALIBRATION`, not proof target.
+- `minor dichotomy`: `CONTINUE`. It is still needed for `u_s>1` branches.
+- `descent lift`: `WAIT`. It matters only after a descended coefficient system
+  survives theorem-(T) tests.
+- `Appendix-II compiler`: `RAISE`. It is the best software shape for theorem
+  (T).
+
+OPEN raised: `OPEN[THEOREM-T]`.
+
+Bounded quantity: first, all descended `s'=2` systems attached to D=108
+full-tree/passport survivors and the Moh Appendix-II `(15,10; X^2)` control;
+second, the D<=200 screened descended types once the compiler is stable.
+
+Cheapest test: use the closed descent-radii formula to generate the
+`gamma,pi` normal form, saturate with positive and negative controls, and
+compare against the repaired Appendix-II case. Do not spend box01 time until
+the desk compiler has a >30-unknown survivor.
+
+OPEN raised: `OPEN[MINOR-DICHOTOMY]`.
+
+Bounded quantity: all promoted screened groups with `u_s>1` up to D<=200, with
+the p.209 branch alternative recorded as typed route data.
+
+Cheapest test: source-read/driver patch only: implement the p.209 branch
+alternatives as labels and rerun the local screen. No Groebner should be used
+until this route data exists.
+
+### Q4 - fresh eyes
+
+Disposition: `NO OUTSIDE MIRACLE; DESIGN THE COEFFICIENT PROOF`.
+
+I do not see a credible mechanism outside boundary/tree/coefficients that is
+stronger than the coefficient computation. Monodromy, dessins, p-adics,
+formal inverse, and PS-growth are all now either filters, diagnostics, or
+ways to package coefficient data. The bold position is that the proof, if this
+campaign is on target, is a uniform coefficient non-realisability theorem for
+full-tree sibling data.
+
+The genuinely new avenue I propose is the `danger-clearing coefficient
+character` test. The full tree allows a dangerous zero part to be neutralized
+only by a typed nonzero sibling choice. In the first live D=108 group, the two
+rows share the top `(10,25,6,4)` node but differ in whether the next selected
+child is zero or nonzero. The coefficient compiler should not merely solve
+each row; it should extract the character/residue contribution of a nonzero
+orbit that clears danger and test whether that contribution can be compatible
+with the child A.3 ODE. If the character is forced nonzero at the parent and
+forced zero at the child, the first live group dies by a new structural rule.
+
+OPEN raised: `OPEN[DANGER-CLEARING-REALISABILITY]`.
+
+Bounded quantity: the two-row D=108 group above, plus any D<=200 survivor group
+with a top zero part and a selected nonzero sibling followed by a selected zero
+child.
+
+Cheapest test: compute the parent cyclic quotient ODE's residue/character
+invariant for `(10,25,6,4)` and compare it with the two child systems
+`(3,7,2,1)` and `(12,28,3,0)`. This is a rank/elimination test before any full
+global moment computation.
+
