+## 5. Reranked bottlenecks
+
+### Proof bottlenecks
+
+1. `OPEN[SIBLING-COEFFICIENTS]`. This is the highest-value bottleneck because
+   it is the first place where promoted necessary tree data can become an
+   actual obstruction. Bounded quantity and cheapest test are in the OPEN
+   register below; the two-row D=108 group is the first target.
+2. `OPEN[DANGER-CLEARING-REALISABILITY]`. This is the first structural lemma I
+   would try to extract from the coefficient compiler. It targets the exact
+   mechanism by which D=108 survived after D=105/D=117 died.
+3. `OPEN[THEOREM-T]`. If sibling coefficients survive locally, theorem (T) is
+   the all-degree local obstruction that can still kill them after descent.
+4. `OPEN[MINOR-DICHOTOMY]`. This is needed for `u_s>1` completeness; without
+   it theorem (T) remains too clean compared with Moh's actual branching.
+5. `OPEN[SCREENED-COFINALITY]`. Important, but I would not spend the first
+   frontier seat here. Its output is a target generator unless it produces a
+   genuine symbolic empty theorem.
+6. `OPEN[TREE-MOMENT-DICTIONARY]`. High value after sibling coefficients;
+   lower value before them because the A2=6 run showed bare moment matrices
+   are not intrinsic.
+7. `OPEN[PASSPORT-SHARPNESS]`. Useful if it closes; not on the shortest proof
+   path.
+8. `OPEN[FULL-TREE-RECENTER]`. Potentially strong, but currently source-thin.
+   It should not outrank the promoted obligations.
+9. `OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM-ARTIFACT]`. Important for historical reconciliation, not
