+8. `OPEN[FULL-TREE-RECENTER]`. Potentially strong, but currently source-thin.
+   It should not outrank the promoted obligations.
+9. `OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM-ARTIFACT]`. Important for historical reconciliation, not
+   a desk-scale proof bottleneck.
+
+### Counterexample bottlenecks
+
+1. Produce a D=108 sibling-coefficient witness for
+   `(108,72), M=(24,78,106), V4=5`. This is the first real adversarial target.
+2. Convert that witness into a legal tree-decorated moment/nonproper-column
+   instance. This blocks false positives from bare interpolation.
+3. Test the descended theorem-(T) monomial-Jacobian pair. A survivor here is a
+   serious counterexample seed; an empty system gives proof information.
+4. Run collision/injectivity ideals on the explicit formal pair. This is the
